<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate dips at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate dips at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell slightly in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said on Monday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	29.85	    -4		29.50     29.90</p>
<p>91-Day	29.46	    -22	     29.30     29.50</p>
<p>182-Day     27.79	    -28	     27.70     27.89</p>
<p>350-Day     26.74				26.61     26.94</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 27.12 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.53 bln pesos     2.81</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   4.41 bln pesos     4.90</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   5.16 bln pesos     5.73</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   2.05 bln pesos     3.42</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.29 compared with 3.38 the week before, on demand of 11.17 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   5  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   4  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 10  basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			 20  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
</text>
